  "memo": "SILICON LOOM - Rabbitoids e2, year 2137. Score 409 vs e1 116 - RANK 1, lead widening ~100/yr from probe spam. Only enabled victory target is planets_owned=60 (I have 4, e1 has 32); minimum_game_time=50 means nothing can be won before 2150, so the game ENDS 2150 and the FINAL SNAPSHOT decides. 13 turns left.\n\nSCORE FORMULA (re-confirmed 2137: built 49 Armed Probes, score 310 -> 409 = +99, i.e. +98 from probes, exact):\n- +2 per armed hull whose DESIGN power_rating <2000; +0.5 per unarmed hull\n- capital ships (>=2000) score (8*C*S)//(C+S) instead - NEVER build one\n- +3 per starbase; +pop//100000 per star; +(sum of every star's res/yr)//30 - that YEAR's output, spending it does NOT reduce it\n- +4 flat once tech >9 (I hold 22) -> RESEARCH BUDGET STAYS 0% FOREVER\nPLANETS SCORE ZERO. Only the final snapshot counts, not accumulated points.\n\nUNIT ECONOMICS: Armed Probe 26 res = 2 pts = 13 res/pt, unbeatable. Pathfinder 34 res/pt, Deep Spore 30, Stalwart Defender 30, Loom Bastion 101, 2nd starbase 133. Home res = factories + pop/1000 (751 + 762 = 1513 confirmed). A factory costs 10 res + 4 Ge and returns 1 res/yr, so with 13 years left it repays ~13 res of probes plus 1/30 pt - still net positive, so ALWAYS top factories and mines to cap FIRST, then dump the rest into Armed Probes.\n\nCAP RULE: mines and factories both cap at pre-growth pop/1000 and both sit AT cap. Queue exactly (cap - built) each year - about 11-14 each - then all remaining resources into Armed Probes. Unspent resources vanish at year end, so over-queue probes slightly.\n\nMINERALS: not binding. 2136->2137 stocks ROSE while building 49 probes: I 2440->2463, B 3853->4165, Ge 718->822. Ironium income ~= 49 probes/yr of demand; the 2463 I buffer absorbs the growing overrun to 2150. No action needed beyond keeping mines at cap.\n\nHOME Zubeneschamali (380,20): pop 762.7k of ~1M, 751/762 fact + 751/762 mine, res 1513/yr, surf 2463 I / 4165 B / 822 Ge. 2137 queue FACTORY 11 / MINE 11 / ARMED PROBE 55.\nZUBENELGENUBI (328,154, 94% hab): pop 56.5k, compounding ~14%/yr toward a 940k cap - projects to ~290-350k pop = ~10-12 pts by 2150 from population alone. No starbase, so it cannot build ships; its 56 res/yr would otherwise VANISH - sink it into MINE 24 (to cap) then FACTORY 20. Re-queue yearly as the cap rises. Ge conc 14 starves factories, hence mines first. Build no new ferries (net negative, re-costed 2136).\nKochab, Gliese 687: dead rocks, 0-2 res, ignore.\n\nWATCH: e1 planet count 32 at 2137, ~+1/turn -> ~45 by 2150, short of 60. If it ever sustains +2/turn, reassess.\n\nDOCTRINE: never colonise; never fight; never build capital ships, defenses or a second starbase; stranded fuel-less scouts still score, leave them idle. Keep all 157+ Armed Probes stacked at home under the starbase - e1 capships = 0 and every raid has been repelled. Stay ENEMY so the starbase fires first. If armed e1 capships appear, split the stack across Zubeneschamali/Kochab and add Stalwart Defenders (they defend AND score 2).",
